[Music]  hi  i am danielle oberdeer the founder of  dekaiodata.com a data science media  company  and the data femme podcast and i'm here  to talk to you  about how content makes our industry  go round and stay connected to one  another  so if you have more questions because  this is a lightning talk  please reach out on twitter at  dekaiodata  or at my site dekaiodata.com i'm always  happy to talk and clarify  more things that i don't get to this  time  so what to make there are several types  of content that you can make when you're  starting out  making content um one obviously  is an audio podcast but that takes a ton  of time  editing finding guests finding sponsors  and it's a lot of work  whereas a blog is not only the amount of  work that you want to make it  you can be amazing like julia silgen do  youtube tutorials  but that is not something within my  expertise i do blog i love it  i love making tutorials that people can  just  look at really quickly without turning  off their tv shows  and just get right to the point i love  writing about  general trends career trends in the  industry um  what's interesting is that long form  content is totally in  average of 1200 words is what is the  most popular  so if you wanna just write content every  month every two months and you have  something to say  know that that long form piece is going  to be something that people  are interested in in terms of where to  share  that's where i just want to give a shout  out to email marketing  email marketing is very important nine  out of ten marketers  um still use email um  to promote their products and 81  of small businesses use email as the  primary way  of connecting with their customers so i  do have an email list  i suggest that if you have a product  that you really want to circulate to  your audience  definitely set up on email there are so  many ways to  set up an email list with your blog i  recommend squarespace and i'm always  available to talk about this like i said  who it helps obviously having content in  our industry really helps bring new  talent  into the folds you can't just expect  to post on linkedin and have all the  right people  get to your message you do have to write  content that is targeted towards people  that might not  feel comfortable addressing certain  issues in the industry  talk to them bring them in um  definitely think about what kind of  content you're addressing  think about um you know current events  and you know it obviously helps  newcomers  it also helps all of us who might not be  newcomers to the field why it matters  well a lot of us don't think about  talking more about content  after our work is over with just a few  packages that we've been working with  all day that you know um our projects  tend to use  if we want to think outside the box and  relate to each other  then the content that we circulate  really fosters that discussion outside  of the workplace  and i think it gives those of us that  are  in higher positions a way to connect  with other people  in other industries who are doing really  good things that they didn't know about  i know that data datafem is often a  connector for  people who never would have met but  listen to the same podcast and then end  up having a discussion  maybe on social media  and here we finally get to how to  succeed  consistency is really important but you  can set the barometer for that you do  not have to  say that consistency means every day it  could mean once a month it could even  mean once a year for certain projects  um really what matters is that  you're consistent about how you promote  your content you're consistent in having  discussions in person at work on social  media  that really matters because that is  really the most important of your  content's  life story is who it reaches and how  so you can make the best content in the  world but if it never reaches anybody  you're not going to really succeed in  the way that  the industry could benefit from  so definitely no matter how much you  write or record make sure  that you're always having conversations  to help you grow your content grow  and the industry grow thank you so much

